{"seconds": 67.8, "exit": 0, "final": "After Nf6+ Kh8 Qxg7+ Kxg7, White doesn't have an immediate way to win material\u2014the rook on f8 still isn't hanging. So the main line is:\n\n**Nf6+ Qxf6 Qxg7+ Kxg7 Rxf6**, winning the queen.\n\nThis is clearly the best move. The motif is a **fork** (the knight move forks the king into a mating net where the queen becomes undefended) combined with an **intermezzo** (Qxg7+ is a check inserted before the expected recapture, winning the hanging queen).\n\nActually, let me reconsider the motif naming. The key move Nf6+ is a check that forces Qxf6 (since Kh8 allows mate threats). Then Qxg7+ is an intermezzo check that wins the queen because it's both check and an attack on f6. So the motif is really the intermezzo\u2014the check inserted into the tactic that wins material.\n\n**Best move: Nf6+**\n\n**Main line: Nf6+ Qxf6 Qxg7+ Kxg7 Rxf6** (winning Black's queen)\n\n**Motif: intermezzo** (check inserted before recapture that wins the hanging piece)\n\n**Explanation:**\nAfter Black's rook move, the queen on e5 is the only defender of f6. Nf6+ forces an immediate response. If Kh8, White has mate threats (Qxg7#). Black must capture with Qxf6. Then Qxg7+ is a check that forces Kxg7, and Rxf6 wins the undefended queen. This gains a full queen in the tactic.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nf6+\", \"line\": [\"Nf6+\", \"Qxf6\", \"Qxg7+\", \"Kxg7\", \"Rxf6\"], \"motifs\": [\"intermezzo\", \"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/5pp1/3p4/p2Nq3/1p2P1Q1/1P6/1P3RKP/4r3 w - - 1 32"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/5pp1/3p4/p2Nq3/1p2P1Q1/1P6/1P3RKP/4r3 w - - 1 32"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/5pp1/3p4/p2Nq3/1p2P1Q1/1P6/1P3RKP/4r3 w - - 1 32"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/5pp1/3p4/p2Nq3/1p2P1Q1/1P6/1P3RKP/4r3 w - - 1 32", "move": "Qxg7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move"